        {
          "path": "_m/d/n/v/h/portsmouth-ohio-wp/coal-chute-door-7983765896.jpg",
          "filename": "Coal Chute Door (7983765896).jpg",
          "caption": "When I saw this along an alley in the Historic Boneyfiddle Disrict of Portsmouth, Ohio, I was reminded of heating with coal at my homeplace. When I got big enough, I helped  Dad shovel coal into our furnace. Coal was dirty but it produced comfortable heat.\nI wonder if anyone else remembers coal heat?\n\n\nThis chute was in the old laundry.",
